%[text] %[text:anchor:T_60E8D80F] # Antiderivatives
%[text] [⇦ Main Menu](file:../../MainMenu.m)
%[text] The rates of change of variables turn up frequently when studying real-life interactions including velocity, acceleration, and current. In cases where we know the derivative and we want to determine the original function, we want to find the *antiderivative.* 
%[text]{"align":"center"} ![A skier sliding down a red cosine curve with a blue sine curve in the background](text:image:0b19)
%[text] By using the knowledge of derivatives, it is possible to define an operation that will undo a derivative. 
%[text:tableOfContents]{"heading":"**Table of Contents**"}
%[text] 
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_51183E7B] **Before you get started:**
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_BF646A47] This live script is intended to be used with the code hidden. On the **View** tab of the MATLAB toolstrip, in the **View** section, select **Hide Code**.  Alternately, select **Hide Code** using the icon ![live script code hidden icon](text:image:880b) at the top right of the Live Editor pane.
%[text] ![Lightbulb mark](text:image:06d0) Although the code is hidden, some interactivity requires familiarity with MATLAB. If you need more instruction, consider taking [MATLAB Onramp](https://matlabacademy.mathworks.com/details/matlab-onramp/gettingstarted), a free 2 hour online tutorial that teaches the essentials of MATLAB.
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_9A4CB605] ## Families of Antiderivatives
%[text] 
%[text]{"align":"center"} $\\displaystyle\\int f(x) \\; dx = F(x) +C,${"altText":"integral of f(x) dx = F(x) +C,"}                       for any constant $C${"altText":"C"}
f = @(x) sin(x); %[control:editfield:06cf]{"position":[9,16]}
  %[control:button:0fcc]{"position":[1,2]}
xVals = -5:.02:5;
syms x
F(x) = int(f,x);
figure %[output:42f4c359]
pfC = DrawFamily(xVals,F(xVals)); %[output:42f4c359]
%%
%[text] To select a particular element of the family, choose a value of $C${"altText":"C"}.
C = 0;  %[control:slider:171f]{"position":[5,6]}
ani = true; %[control:checkbox:8446]{"position":[7,11]}
if ~exist("pfC","var")
    xVals = -5:.02:5;
    syms x
    f(x) = sin(x); % Setting default values
    F(x) = int(f,x);
    figure
    pfC = DrawFamily(xVals,F(xVals));
end
if ani %[output:group:15151733]
    % Identify maximum and minimum values range of plotted family members to
    % determine a reasonable window
    Fx = double(F(xVals)); 
    FxMin = min(Fx);
    FxMax = max(Fx);
    pfC.Parent.YLim = [FxMin FxMax] + [-10 10]; %[output:8d15914a]

    % Animate the plot
    for C = [-10:.25:10 10:-.25:-10]
        pfC.YData = Fx + C; %[output:8d15914a]
        subtitle(pfC.Parent,"$C = $"+C,"Interpreter","latex");
        drawnow
    end
else
    pfC.YData = F(xVals)+C; 
    subtitle(pfC.Parent,"$C = $"+C,"Interpreter","latex");
end %[output:group:15151733]
drawnow
